## Where things are documented

`docs/index.md` is the navigator over every doc, module README, report, and
skill — with status, audience, and an **Authority & precedence** order. Start
there; it routes, the linked target is the SSOT. Rules worth internalizing
without a hop:

- `docs/rules/` holds portable doctrine (kit-owned): `governance.md` (repo
  governance, symlink layout, kit propagation), `authoring.md` (profile-scoped
  technical prose), `doc.md` (doc lifecycle), `python.md` (code style),
  `skill.md` (skill authoring), and `testing.md`.
- `docs/glossary/` is the ubiquitous-language SSOT; code names must match it, and
  a new domain term updates the glossary in the same change.
- `readme.md` / `README.md` is human setup + usage.

## Working principles

- **Concise is the key.**
- **Full means full.** When asked to complete, extend, or verify coverage, do the
  actual work — never relabel a partial run as "full".
- **Verify before claiming done.** After any change, run the full suite *and* lint
  (`make test` / `make lint`) green before reporting. Numeric claims are
  re-checked against the code, not quoted from memory.
- **Symlinks are load-bearing** (see below). Verify link targets before `rm` or
  bulk file ops near them.

## Implementation records

Every `IMPLEMENT` task names one primary file under `records/work-items/items/`. Before
changing implementation surfaces, transition it to `wip` and append its Status
History. Append material findings, assumptions, decisions, deviations,
verification, and handoff information directly to its Implementation Ledger; do
not leave them only in chat or a separate report. At the stop condition, update
the item to `done`, `partial`, `blocked`, or leave it `wip` with an explicit
handoff. Closing as `partial` requires linked residual backlog items.

## Agent toolchains & symlink layout

This repo is worked by multiple agent toolchains sharing one source of truth by
symlink, not copy — full layout and rationale in `docs/rules/governance.md`.
INVARIANT: `.codex/` holds the real assets; `.agents` and `.claude/skills` are
**relative symlinks into it** (declared in `[tool.doc_governance.symlinks]`,
verified by lint, created/repaired by `scripts/bootstrap_agents.py`). Create/edit
skills only under `.codex/skills/` — never duplicate per toolchain.

