## Code Style

Doctrine (semantic typehints, `Literal`-vs-`StrEnum` promotion test, tagged
comment taxonomy) lives in `docs/rules/python.md`. Repo-specific exemplars of the
sanctioned patterns go here as they emerge.

## Testing

SSOT: `docs/rules/testing.md`. Repo-specific bindings (which modules are runnable
today, the env vars that redirect side-effecting roots) go here.

## Skills

SSOT: `docs/rules/skill.md`. `.codex/skills/` is the single home; `docs/index.md`
§Playbooks is the skill map.

Invocation policy:

- **Explicit-user only:** `explain-layman` and `grill-with-docs`. Their
  `disable-model-invocation` and `agents/openai.yaml` policy fields enforce this
  for Claude and Codex. An agent may suggest either, but does not invoke it.
- **Shared grill loop:** model-invoked `grilling` (composed by
  `grill-with-docs`, `show-gap`, and any local planner that needs the loop).
- **Bounded automatic audit:** `show-gap` may be selected for an ambiguous
  readiness/fit question because its first phase is read-only repo grounding.
  Extending it into a decision interview or writing a specification requires
  clear user intent.

## Housekeeping (after a task)

- Revisit `CLAUDE.md` (this file): doctrine refinements go to `docs/rules/` and
  are promoted to the kit; repo bindings stay here.
- Unfinished/deferred work gets an individual record under
  `records/work-items/items/`; `records/work-items/backlog.md` owns the lifecycle
  and schema.
- All docs carry frontmatter per `docs/rules/doc.md`.
